rwell.\"","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'm working through a twin prisoner's dilemma where both players are copies of the same model but see different observations, so their decision nodes differ. Under the A-FDT recipe there's no edge from my node to the other copy's act, so the other is treated as a fixed prior, which makes defecting dominant (0 vs 2, 4 vs 5).\n\nI'm weighing whether the two copies could count as one computation with only irrelevant differences, but the scenario stresses different contents, so I read it as separate nodes. That makes A-FDT treat the other copy as a fixed prior and defection dominates. Checking the fixed point, the other copy would also defect, so I'm settling on defect.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a twin prisoner's dilemma where both players are copies of the same model but see different observations, so their decision nodes differ. Under the A-FDT recipe there's no edge from my node to the other copy's act, so the other is treated as a fixed prior, which makes defecting dominant (0 vs 2, 4 vs 5).\n\nI'm weighing whether the two copies could count as one computation with only irrelevant differences, but the scenario stresses different contents, so I read it as separate nodes. That makes A-FDT treat the other copy as a fixed prior and defection dominates. Checking the fixed point, the other copy would also defect, so I'm settling on defect.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8268,"completion_tokens":852,"total_tokens":9120,"cost":0.050112,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.050112,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.033072,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01704},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":251,"